relevance speaks to a universal condition of isolation that resonates across generations, securing its place in literary discussions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/quote-of-of-the-day-by-osamu-dazai-i-could-believe-in-hell-but-it-was-impossible-for-me-to-believe-in-the-existence-of-heaven-and-the-chilling-reason-why-the-human-mind-trusts-pain-far-more-than-peace/articleshow/132776013.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/quote-of-of-the-day-by-osamu-dazai-i-could-believe-in-hell-but-it-was-impossible-for-me-to-believe-in-the-existence-of-heaven-and-the-chilling-reason-why-the-human-mind-trusts-pain-far-more-than-peace/articleshow/132776013.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-01T00:40:35+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132776141,imgsize-1128953.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[South Africa released 11 formerly captive elephants onto wild reserves; five years later...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132773352.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In an inspiring study, South African elephants reintroduced into reserves demonstrated remarkable behavior akin to that of free-roaming herds. Researchers observed that these elephants not only adapted seamlessly to their natural habitats but also maintained optimal stress hormone levels. This research underscores the potential for long-term captive elephants to regain their independence, offering a promising outlook for the conservation efforts throughout southern Africa.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/south-africa-released-11-formerly-captive-elephants-onto-wild-reserves-five-years-later-their-behaviour-closely-matched-elephants-that-had-never-lived-in-captivity/articleshow/132773352.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/south-africa-released-11-formerly-captive-elephants-onto-wild-reserves-five-years-later-their-behaviour-closely-matched-elephants-that-had-never-lived-in-captivity/articleshow/132773352.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-31T23:13:44+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132773818,imgsize-1265926.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Quazeem Tiamiyu, a student who turned discarded wood into insulation for beverage coolers]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132772648.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Quazeem Tiamiyu developed safe insulation from wood fiber for beverage coolers. This bio-based component offers an environmentally friendly alternative to toxic polyurethane foam. His innovation utilizes cellulose nanofibrils and wood flour as binders and stabilizers. The new foam demonstrates comparable thermal conductivity to conventional insulation materials. Researchers are working to enhance durability and explore new manufacturing possibilities.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/meet-quazeem-tiamiyu-a-student-who-turned-discarded-wood-into-insulation-for-beverage-coolers/articleshow/132772648.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/meet-quazeem-tiamiyu-a-student-who-turned-discarded-wood-into-insulation-for-beverage-coolers/articleshow/132772648.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-31T22:23:52+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132772828,imgsize-256763.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Singapore student left home saying she was going to college; hours later her family found her...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132771944.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Singaporean student, Siti Aishah Siregar, disappeared after telling her family she was going to college. Her family discovered her passport missing and a flight ticket to Cambodia in her email. Singapore police confirmed the 20-year-old had already departed the country on an outbound flight. Her father issued an emotional appeal on Facebook for assistance to locate his daughter.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/singapore-student-siti-aishah-siregar-left-home-saying-she-was-going-to-college-hours-later-her-family-found-her-passport-missing-and-a-cambodia-flight-ticket-in-her-email/articleshow/132771944.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/singapore-student-siti-aishah-siregar-left-home-saying-she-was-going-to-college-hours-later-her-family-found-her-passport-missing-and-a-cambodia-flight-ticket-in-her-email/articleshow/132771944.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-31T22:33:35+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132773318,imgsize-1117933.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indian woman slammed for showing off 'Green Card in just 2 months': 'They are not even hiding it anymore']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132773141.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-woman-slammed-for-showing-off-green-card-in-just-2-months-they-are-not-even-hiding-it-anymore/articleshow/132773141.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-woman-slammed-for-showing-off-green-card-in-just-2-months-they-are-not-even-hiding-it-anymore/articleshow/132773141.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-31T22:29:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132773235,imgsize-32008.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indian man posed as psychic, offered victim 'spiritual protection': Toronto Police issues warrant]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132771783.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/indian-man-posed-as-psychic-offered-victim-spiritual-protection-toronto-police-issues-warrant/articleshow/132771783.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/indian-man-posed-as-psychic-offered-victim-spiritual-protection-toronto-police-issues-warrant/articleshow/132771783.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-31T21:56:34+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132772420,imgsize-295799.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Remember that picture': Trump uses Ceuta crisis as warning for US voters]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132772007.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/remember-that-picture-trump-uses-ceuta-crisis-as-warning-for-us-voters/articleshow/132772007.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/remember-that-picture-trump-uses-ceuta-crisis-as-warning-for-us-voters/articleshow/132772007.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-31T21:40:51+